                <pb facs="0321" n="223" xml:id="pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11330: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-20T13:00:00+08:00">December 20, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 20—9:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>139. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 20, 1 p.m. It is definitely established that Tsingshih, Honan,
                            was occupied for the second time by the communist army under Ho Lung
                            from December 1 to 9, during which time a large number of gentry and
                            rich people were ruthlessly killed and extensive pillage and looting
                            [apparent omission]. Standard Oil Company lost 6,000 units of oil.</p>
                        <p>Steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Chi Chuen</hi> of Yangtze Rapid Company
                            heavily fired upon at several places between Chenglingki and Shasi by
                            rifle fire and trench mortars on 16th and 17th. Naval armed guard aboard
                            returned fire. Vessels arriving here today in passing through same
                            stretch of river yesterday and day before not fired upon.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to the Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
